gent-Field/CodeAF/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-05T16:00:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:31:44Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-23T18:17:10Z","git_url":"git://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF","homepage":"http://agentfield.ai/","size":196153,"stargazers_count":116,"watchers_count":116,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":14,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":141,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-fleet","agent-harness","agentfield","agentic-coding","ai","ai-coding","cli-agent","coding-agent","coding-agents","coding-assistant","coding-cli","coding-harness","developer-tools","harness","harness-engineering","llm","open-models","open-source-models","software-factory","terminal-agent"],"visibility":"public","forks":14,"open_issues":141,"watchers":116,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls/1410","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1410","diff_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1410.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1410.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Brings `santos/dev2` onto `dev`. dev is already merged in with a real merge commit, so this is a fast-forward: dev has nothing that dev2 lacks.\n\n**Status: draft.** The review fixes listed under \"Still landing\" are going into dev2 now. This PR follows them automatically and goes ready when they are in.\n\n## What this brings\n\n**1. The worker harness, now the default.** A task runs on a bash belt: one loop under both `/task` and `codeaf do`, with a checking seat for the belt check. `CODEAF_TASK_BELT=node` (or `legacy`, or `off`) is the way back to the older node belt. See #1109 waves 1, 2, 6 and 7, and #1335, #1340, #1355, #1207.\n\n**2. Runs as first-class work.**\n- A run's life is the conversation's.\n- It works in its own copy, and the copy is written down so it can be found again.\n- Dollar and time limits end it by one road, and the ending names the limit that caused it.\n- A run's dollars reach the conversation's total.\n- Work that nothing is driving reads as interrupted, not failed, and can be carried on.\n- A stopped task reads stopped everywhere.\n\nAbout 50 entries, from #1204 through #1305.\n\n**3. Skills, first design (to be replaced).** A memory-backed shelf, `use_skill`, per-message automatic choice, a `/skill` picker that attaches a skill, and a report of which skills a turn used (#1327, #1345–#1348, #1380). This follows the first design in #1277. #1409 builds the settled plan on dev and replaces these pieces after this lands; see the note on #1409.\n\n**4. The chat as manager over the plan store.** The chat role. The chat sees the plan when the person speaks, and notes are a channel into a running worker. See #1205, #1354, #1356 and #1357.\n\n**5. Task page, rail and step rows.** The page and rail door. Step rows are cut from the commands as they ran, step numbers continue across a wake, and a call that did not run has no row. See #1231, #1257, #1260 and #1261.\n\n**6. Pickers.** One fuzzy matcher for every picker, match highlighting, and the caret parks where you type (#1321).\n\n**7. Benchmarks and docs.** The footprint benchmark and its method, resume cost (#1126, #1317), and ADHD-shaped answers (#1209).\n\n**8. Hardening.**\n- Heavy-suite locks as kernel file locks (#1264, #1270, #1284, #1324).\n- Goroutine ownership at close (#1259, #1267, #1274, #1276).\n- Unread and retired profile keys (#1223, #1245).\n- The CI gate on this branch (#1362).\n\n## Behaviour that changes on merge\n\n- **Tasks run on the bash belt by default.** Before, `CODEAF_TASK_BELT=bash` opted in. Now `node`, `legacy` or `off` opts out.\n- `task.parallel` = 0 means no limit on both doors.\n\n## Review\n\nEvery feature group above had a feature-level review against its change entry. The findings are being fixed in their own PRs into dev2, each with tests shown failing first and a full `make check` on the merged head.\n\nAlready in:\n- #1411: run lifecycle (10 findings). A new request never adopts an earlier run, every ending is written on the root, the dollar limit ends peers, close lands nothing, steers on ended runs are refused, interrupted rows are honest.\n- #1393: chat manager (9 findings). The digest leads with the live run in the rail's words, `say` and `forward` reach run rows, a key that is read is no longer reported unread, and `Assisted-by` follows `/model`.\n- #1395: task page keys, the tab mark, pool judge sweep claims, unowned catalog warms, manual gaps (12 findings).\n- The dev merge: a parked parent could wake before its child's review check was seated. Fixed in `internal/run`, 100 stress runs green.\n\nStill landing:\n- **`codeaf do`.** It must never commit work it did not make. Spend stays bounded unless the person says otherwise. Project `*.lock` files land.\n- **Retry loop.** A server that keeps cutting its answer short is waited on, not re-asked in a tight loop. \"One machine\" applies only when routing is actually off.\n- **Attribution.** Always on: every commit codeaf writes carries `Assisted-by: CodeAF (<model>)` then `Co-Authored-By`. The model is shown as its bare name, with no provider prefix, and it is the one part a person can turn off.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The merge of dev into dev2 at `525b77fde`: full `make check` EXIT 0, including the Windows cross-builds. Nothing is on the known-red list.\n- #1395 at `635c029c6`, #1393 at `449e7921c`, #1411 at `888911c05`: full `make check` EXIT 0 each. CI green on each.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1410/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]